{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial","id":1506256,"title":"Raising Spheres when you\u2019re antisocial ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-23T12:38:05-07:00","id":1506256,"title":"Raising Spheres when you\u2019re antisocial ?","content":"I seem to remember that RAW in the Core state that you can\u2019t raise your spheres without a mage teacher, ideally one that shares your paradigm. Spirit Mentors can\u2019t help you. Library lets you research rotes but not raise spheres (though a while back, I got some very good suggestions on this forum on houserules to change that).<br /> <br /> I was wondering if that had changed in recent books. I think a suitably powerful grimoire like the one in Book of the Fallen would allow it, but are there other possibilities? How do Orphans or Solitaires go about improving their spheres ?<br /> <br /> I know I can houserule it. I just wanted to know if anything new changed in the RAW.<br /> <br /> Thanks !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T04:01:25-07:00","id":1506299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial#post1506256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do Orphans or Solitaires go about improving their spheres ?<br /> <br /> I know I can houserule it. I just wanted to know if anything new changed in the RAW.<br /> <br /> Thanks !</div> </div> </div> </div>A Mage from one of the Nine Mystical Traditions ( For example Choristers, Hermetics, or Virtual Adepts ) or a Technocrat ( From the Syndicate or the Progenitors, to name at least two Conventions of the Technocracy ) could very well help another Mage that does not have same or comparable Paradigm and attitude. With enough good work and honest optimism results could be achieved. It has to be noted that raising Sphere level is not neccesirely the only desired and positive outcome. In regard to this there is certainly the possibility of additional personal ambitions, goals, and objectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T07:17:30-07:00","id":1506305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506299#post1506299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Mage from one of the Nine Mystical Traditions ( For example Choristers, Hermetics, or Virtual Adepts ) or a Technocrat ( From the Syndicate or the Progenitors, to name at least two Conventions of the Technocracy ) could very well help another Mage that does not have same or comparable Paradigm and attitude. With enough good work and honest optimism results could be achieved. It has to be noted that raising Sphere level is not neccesirely the only desired and positive outcome. In regard to this there is certainly the possibility of additional personal ambitions, goals, and objectives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you say, but that\u2019s not my question. What I\u2019m asking is if there is any way for a mage to raise their spheres other than \u201cYou need someone else to teach you\u201d. Solitary practitioners seem to have no way to improve on their own per the RAW aside from grimoires, and I wanted to know if I\u2019d just missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T07:22:52-07:00","id":1506306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial#post1506256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember that RAW in the Core state that you can\u2019t raise your spheres without a mage teacher, ideally one that shares your paradigm. Spirit Mentors can\u2019t help you. Library lets you research rotes but not raise spheres (though a while back, I got some very good suggestions on this forum on houserules to change that).<br /> <br /> I was wondering if that had changed in recent books. I think a suitably powerful grimoire like the one in Book of the Fallen would allow it, but are there other possibilities? How do Orphans or Solitaires go about improving their spheres ?<br /> <br /> I know I can houserule it. I just wanted to know if anything new changed in the RAW.<br /> <br /> Thanks !</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not really correct. You can raise your spheres without a teacher through experimentation and self work. At the end of the day, your Avatar is always with you and it can help make discoveries or point you in the right direction. Otherwise noone would ever be a Mage outside the Traditions and the Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T07:39:47-07:00","id":1506309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506306#post1506306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not really correct. You can raise your spheres without a teacher through experimentation and self work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the sentiment \u2026 but I couldn\u2019t find anything in the RAW for Mage20 to support it. That\u2019s why I\u2019m asking. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T07:51:56-07:00","id":1506310,"title":"","content":"Assuming we are talking about this:<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raising or Learning Spheres, M20 Core, pg 337</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In order to learn a new Sphere, or improve the ones you have, your mage will need to study with someone whose magickal focus is more or less the same as your character's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we can read that as a hard rule. Three sentences later the text says that mages can learn from different sects, it just takes longer. Clearly &quot;need&quot; is not meant as an absolute in this context. Further, the Library Background specifically says it helps characters research Spheres, which opens up the possibility that Mages don't need a mentor at all. <br /> <br /> That interpretation has the added bonus of being consistent with previous editions (if I recall correctly) and of actually making sense. The existence of Orphans heavily implies that magic can be learned without help. Also, mentors need to get their knowledge from somewhere. It's probably not mentors all the way down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T08:22:59-07:00","id":1506311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506309#post1506309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with the sentiment \u2026 but I couldn\u2019t find anything in the RAW for Mage20 to support it. That\u2019s why I\u2019m asking.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're not going to get far in life with Mage if you just go by what's in RAW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Consider that you have Orphans and people who never were a part of any tradition, or people who were say practitioners of certain faiths who learned their own magic through practicing their own religion? How do you even imagine Traditions and Crafts started if everyone had to be taught from a teacher within the same set of tools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T09:09:16-07:00","id":1506312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506311#post1506311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not going to get far in life with Mage if you just go by what's in RAW <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Consider that you have Orphans and people who never were a part of any tradition, or people who were say practitioners of certain faiths who learned their own magic through practicing their own religion? How do you even imagine Traditions and Crafts started if everyone had to be taught from a teacher within the same set of tools?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, I agree. Whether you play a lonely Orphan figuring things out the hard way for lack of an alternative, or a cantankerous Hermetic from House Bonisagus who enjoys researching the spheres in his remote sanctum, free from the bothersome inaneness of dealing with people, personal progress through research, study, and practice should be a thing.<br /> <br /> A teacher would absolutely help, but it shouldn\u2019t be mandatory. <br /> <br /> When M20 came put, I thought the Library nerf was nonsensical and that a mage teacher being mandatory made no sense, but I thought maybe they\u2019d eventually address that in one of the supplements. I just didn\u2019t know if they did.<br /> <br /> Hence my question. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T09:15:39-07:00","id":1506313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506310#post1506310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming we are talking about this:<br /> <br /> I don't think we can read that as a hard rule. Three sentences later the text says that mages can learn from different sects, it just takes longer. Clearly &quot;need&quot; is not meant as an absolute in this context. Further, the Library Background specifically says it helps characters research Spheres, which opens up the possibility that Mages don't need a mentor at all.<br /> <br /> That interpretation has the added bonus of being consistent with previous editions (if I recall correctly) and of actually making sense. The existence of Orphans heavily implies that magic can be learned without help. Also, mentors need to get their knowledge from somewhere. It's probably not mentors all the way down.</div> </div> </div> </div>It did seem pretty definitive, but I suppose you can interpret the \u201cyour mage will need to study with someone\u200b\u201c as unfortunate phrasing. Was an errata for the Core ever released ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T10:42:35-07:00","id":1506319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trianoma4Evah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506313#post1506313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It did seem pretty definitive, but I suppose you can interpret the \u201cyour mage will need to study with someone\u200b\u201c as unfortunate phrasing. Was an errata for the Core ever released ?</div> </div> </div> </div>None that I am aware of.<br /> <br /> It is indeed unfortunate phrasing in a game book. In general we are quite good at telling the difference between absolute and relative need. If a college student said he needed to find someone to teach him X, we would certainly understand he was capable of learning it other ways. If I said I needed a car to get to Oregon... well there's a series of video games based around a time when people walked there.<br /> <br /> In a game book, though, we expect more definite and absolute statements, so much so that we have a hard time letting go of them. It doesn't make sense that a mage would absolutely need a mentor to learn Spheres, but Mage doesn't always make sense, so it is harder to reject the interpretation even when we have good reason to think it is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":".  Forgot a line 03-24-2023, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T12:26:33-07:00","id":1506335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1506319#post1506319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ***very good point***</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I\u2019m going with your interpretation. It makes much more sense. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26426-trianoma4evah","name":"Trianoma4Evah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T05:04:34-08:00","id":1546859,"title":"","content":"Gona do some necromancy here.<br /> <br /> What if the character is not a reasercher (frawns on books) and does not have a mentor? Can he learn in other ways? For example from an Avatar?<br /> <br /> How would you do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T05:50:23-08:00","id":1546861,"title":"","content":"As said, the text in M20 can't be taken as a hard rule, if it get's contradicted one paragraph latter, and then again on Library, and it doesn't make sense with Orphans being a thing. That being the case, there's no hard rule about learning Spheres other than spending XP to them as usual.<br /> <br /> I dare say that, accepting this as a premise, we could say mages learn from the experience gained by acting in accordance with their Focus. So: Do anything that suits your Focus. Learn in dreams (Dream?) as divine revelation, relive your Past Lives and their legacy of kung-fu at the top of the mountain, learn from interaction with spirits (there is a whole camp of Dreamspeakers that are basically orphans taught by spirits)...or whatever suits the character best.<br /> <br /> If a mage wants to <i>really </i>explore the &quot;route&quot; of learning stuff from their Avatar to the fullest, I would say to take Manifest Avatar Merit, Mentor, and say the mentor it's the Avatar...<br /> <br /> <br /> You won't have any bonuses from learning that way, tho, you need a Grimmoire (or another kind of &quot;special&quot; rule) for that. That's an advantage of being part of a faction, and study (note that, in spite of the name, not all Grimmoires need to be books as per 20th, so the form of that &quot;study&quot; may vary)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-11-2024, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T13:25:34-08:00","id":1546875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1506256-raising-spheres-when-you\u2019re-antisocial?p=1546859#post1546859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gona do some necromancy here.<br /> <br /> What if the character is not a reasercher (frawns on books) and does not have a mentor? Can he learn in other ways? For example from an Avatar?<br /> <br /> How would you do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>He can learn by trial and mistake, no need of books.<br /> <br /> Let's remember, every single Magic group that exists today didn't exist at some point. To each one of them, there has to be a founder or group of founders that first codified their principles.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Avatar can teach, and so can trial and mistake. The Mage contracts his sphincter pretty tight, trying to make something happen... And nothing will happen - until it does.<br /> <br /> It is that simple actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-11T18:39:34-08:00","id":1546885,"title":"","content":"If you're going with M20, there is a type of Wonder referred to as a Grimoire, and some of those can be used to learn Spheres.<br /> <br /> I haven't had this possibility come up in one of my games, but if a character were to come to an arrangement with a very powerful spirit of the appropriate type, I <i>might </i>allow them to form a student/teacher relationship one. It would have to be something on the same level as a powerful demon (those <i>can </i>teach knowledge of the Spheres, if a character fancies becoming a nephandus) and while a mage might not necessarily have to sell their soul for the privilege, the spirit will certainly require some sort of serious pact or major service in exchange for the tutelage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28664-steve-bridger","name":"Steve Bridger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}